&lt;h3&gt;About Manifest&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manifest is on a mission to secure the global software and AI supply chain. Our platform automates the discovery and analysis of risks across internally built and third-party software and AI systems, giving security, product, and engineering teams complete visibility into the components and dependencies that make up their technology stack. From product security and AI risk to supplier risk and compliance, we help teams trust the software and AI they build and buy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded by alumni from the Department of Defense, CISA, and Palantir, Manifest is backed by leading investors including Ensemble VC, First Round Capital, Homebrew, BoxGroup, XYZ Venture Capital, AE Ventures, Leap435, and Overmatch VC. The company partners with the US Air Force, DHS, Global 2000 companies, and critical infrastructure organizations across defense, automotive, and financial services to bring transparency, resilience, and trust to modern digital systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a resourceful, highly organized Business Operations Associate who can turn ideas into action. You&#39;ll own projects across people operations, recruiting, vendors, systems, and company operations that keep the business moving forward. You’ll serve as connective tissue across the organization, partnering with teams to drive high-impact initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right person is a generalist with a high bar for execution: someone who learns quickly, brings structure to ambiguous problems, follows through on the details, and is comfortable taking on things they haven’t done before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique opportunity to gain broad, cross-functional exposure at a category-defining startup, where your work directly shapes the company’s ability to scale. You’ll see firsthand how a startup operates, from People and Finance to go-to-market, product, company planning, and leadership decisions. The role is built to grow with you: as you build context and earn trust, you’ll take on bigger, higher-impact work, including broader business and finance operations. It’s a strong fit for someone who wants to learn how to run a company from the inside and grow into a startup leader. You&#39;ll report to the Head of Operations, who sets the goals and the end result. You turn those into a plan, coordinate the right people, and see it through, flagging issues early and bringing decisions forward with a well-evidenced recommendation attached. Over time, you&#39;ll become the go-to expert on how the company runs and build relationships across every team, so you can move quickly and cross-functionally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities include, but are not limited to:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business operations and planning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather and analyze operational data to surface insights that support leadership decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive special projects, managing timelines, stakeholders, and deliverables across Finance, Legal, IT, and other partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own onboarding and offboarding, and be the first stop for employee questions on benefits, policies, and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run compliance processes, including employee data collection, required trainings, insurance, and audit documentation, and track recurring deadlines like state filings and renewals so nothing slips&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own vendors and tools: hold partners accountable, manage invoices, renewals, and contracts, and implement integrations that replace manual work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead offsites and events coordination end to end, and handle hands-on logistics like shipping equipment, swag, and gifts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep documentation, trackers, and checklists clear, current, and scalable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide executive support to the leadership team, including scheduling, travel, and meeting logistics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the company’s operating rhythm, including planning cycles, budget tracking, headcount, and reporting, and help prepare materials for leadership reviews, board meetings, and fundraising&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process and systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build internal processes where none exist, then automate them with AI and the right tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build dashboards and integrate and consolidate tools so the team works from clean, connected sources of truth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build alignment across teams and turn decisions into working processes and make sure the team follows them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring clear, well-supported recommendations forward and present them persuasively to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot growing pains before they become problems, and fix them proactively behind the scenes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of new priorities and close gaps across the business as they emerge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finance operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own accounts payable, receivable, and reconciliations so the books stay accurate and timely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain trusted sources of truth for operational and financial data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in a complex, fast-moving environment with little day-to-day direction. Operations, implementation, chief of staff, consulting, or corporate roles all count, and we&#39;d love to hear from people moving from corporate into tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong execution skills. You&#39;re organized, dependable, and detail-oriented, and you can take a goal, build the plan, and see it through without step-by-step management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive approach. You spot what needs to happen and take initiative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment about priorities, tradeoffs, and when to ask for help, including with confidential employee and company information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-quality deliverables and clear written and verbal communication with leaders, vendors, and candidates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An AI-native, critical approach, with proven experience using AI and automation to build dashboards, consolidate tools, and design systems that improve how a company operates. You pressure-test AI output and apply your own judgment, so you can defend every recommendation yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with systems and data, plus the curiosity to learn new tools and unfamiliar topics quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working through ambiguity and shifting priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, low-ego attitude and a willingness to do hands-on work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with tools like Rippling, QuickBooks, HubSpot, and AI platforms such as Claude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to accounts payable and receivable or other finance operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with offsite or event planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A project management or process improvement certification, such as PMP or Lean Six Sigma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $ 80,000 - $110,000, plus equity. Final compensation is commensurate with experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully remote&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO (taken seriously)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance — 100% covered for you and your dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) and retirement options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;About Manifest&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manifest is on a mission to secure the global software and AI supply chain. Our platform automates the discovery and analysis of risks across internally built and third-party software and AI systems, giving security, product, and engineering teams complete visibility into the components and dependencies that make up their technology stack. From product security and AI risk to supplier risk and compliance, we help teams trust the software and AI they build and buy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded by alumni from the Department of Defense, CISA, and Palantir, Manifest is backed by leading investors including Ensemble VC, First Round Capital, Homebrew, BoxGroup, XYZ Venture Capital, AE Ventures, Leap435, and Overmatch VC. The company partners with the US Air Force, DHS, Global 2000 companies, and critical infrastructure organizations across defense, automotive, and financial services to bring transparency, resilience, and trust to modern digital systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Customer Success Engineer at Manifest Cyber, you will own the post-sale relationship for a portfolio of large enterprise and government customers, ensuring they realize measurable value from the Manifest platform from onboarding through renewal and expansion.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Head of Business Operations, you&#39;ll act as a trusted advisor on software supply chain security and AI risk, working closely with security, engineering, GRC, and procurement stakeholders at some of the most highly regulated organizations in the world. This role requires someone comfortable operating in technical conversations, navigating complex enterprise and federal customer environments, and translating customer needs into product and account strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own onboarding, adoption, and renewal for a portfolio of large enterprise and government accounts, serving as the primary point of contact after the sale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop deep relationships with customer stakeholders across security, engineering, compliance/GRC, and procurement, and map their goals to Manifest&#39;s platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product adoption by helping customers configure code and dependency scanning tools in CI/CD pipelines, vulnerability management workflows, and third-party risk workflows that fit their environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor account health, proactively identify risk of churn or underutilization, and build action plans to address it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales on expansion opportunities and provide input on account strategy for your book of business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the voice of the customer internally, relaying feedback to Product and Engineering to influence the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain customer-facing materials, including onboarding plans, business reviews, and success plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot technical questions independently where possible, working with databases, APIs, and JSON-based data (including SBOM/AIBOM/CryptographyBOM formats like SPDX and CycloneDX), and looping in Engineering or Support when deeper investigation is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use basic scripting to investigate data issues, validate integrations, or build lightweight reporting for customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply frontier AI tools to work more efficiently, such as drafting customer communications, summarizing account activity, analyzing data, and researching customer environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel periodically to meet with customers on-site, with particular focus on the greater Washington, D.C. area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in a customer success, account management, or similar customer-facing role, ideally supporting large enterprise customers with complex, multi-stakeholder relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting U.S. government customers, particularly within the federal civilian sector, including familiarity with how government agencies evaluate, procure, and operationalize software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record in cybersecurity and/or SaaS customer success, including driving adoption, managing renewals, and reducing churn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical skills:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Comfort working with technical systems and data, including relational databases, REST APIs, and JSON schemas, with the ability to read and troubleshoot at a working technical level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write basic scripts (e.g., Python, shell, or similar) to investigate issues, automate small tasks, or support reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with software supply chain security concepts, including Software Bills of Materials (SBOMs) and AI Bills of Materials (AIBOMs), and standards such as SPDX and CycloneDX.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort using frontier AI models (e.g., Claude, ChatGPT, or similar) as part of daily workflow to troubleshoot integrations, fix poorly formatted BOMs, and improve efficiency and quality of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate technical concepts for both highly technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple accounts and priorities simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidates must be based in or willing to relocate to the greater Washington, D.C. area.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Citizenship is required for this role.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice To Haves&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active security clearance or the ability to obtain and maintain one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with vulnerability management, GRC, or third-party risk management workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;$130,000–$175,000 base, plus performance-based bonus and stock options. Final base depends on experience and location skills&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help organizations get new-found visibility into their software, and be more secure!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully remote work (with potential for hybrid co-working)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO (which we take seriously)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% medical/dental/vision insurance coverage for you and your dependents!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) and retirement options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help get in at the ground floor of a well-funded, early-stage startup!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, mission-driven team built from diverse backgrounds across national security, defense, enterprise technology, and beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;About Manifest&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manifest is on a mission to secure the global software and AI supply chain. Our platform automates the discovery and analysis of risks across internally built and third-party software and AI systems, giving security, product, and engineering teams complete visibility into the components and dependencies that make up their technology stack. From product security and AI risk to supplier risk and compliance, we help teams trust the software and AI they build and buy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded by alumni from the Department of Defense, CISA, and Palantir, Manifest is backed by leading investors including Ensemble VC, First Round Capital, Homebrew, BoxGroup, XYZ Venture Capital, AE Ventures, Leap435, and Overmatch VC. The company partners with the US Air Force, DHS, Global 2000 companies, and critical infrastructure organizations across defense, automotive, and financial services to bring transparency, resilience, and trust to modern digital systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manifest is hiring an Enterprise Account Executive to own the federal civilian market. This is a quota-carrying individual contributor role covering only civilian agencies. You will report to the Head of Federal Sales and carry a number from your first full quarter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There is no BDR team. There is no one who will hand you a list, book your meetings, or build your account plan. You will source the majority of your own pipeline, and finding a program office with an SBOM problem and a budget line will be work you do yourself. You will also be the person who builds the account map, writes the RFI response, chases the contracting officer, and closes the deal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You already know how federal civilian agencies actually buy. You understand that a signed evaluation and an enthusiastic champion are not a deal, that the money moves through a vehicle and a contracting officer, and that a program office&#39;s fiscal-year clock will shape your close date more than your urgency will. You know the difference between a technical win and a funded requirement, and you have worked on both sides often enough to sequence them correctly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You also know the space. You will be in rooms with agency CISOs, program security leads, and the engineers who will actually run the product, and you need to hold a credible conversation about software supply chain risk, SBOM and AIBOM, vulnerability management, and the regulatory drivers behind them. We will teach you Manifest. The fundamentals of the category and the mechanics of federal procurement you bring with you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work alongside the Head of Federal Sales, sales engineering, and marketing, and receive real support from all three. This is a high-ownership seat at an early-stage company, and the line between your work and the company&#39;s growth is short and visible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quota and Self-Sourced Pipeline. Carry and deliver an annual number. Source the majority of your own pipeline through direct outbound, agency events, partner-led introductions, and your existing network. Prospecting is not a phase you graduate out of once you have coverage; it is a weekly discipline you will be held to alongside bookings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Territory and Account Planning. Build and maintain a written account plan for the federal civilian territory, including named target agencies, component-level entry points, incumbent tooling, and the funded programs where supply chain security is already a requirement. Likely targets given our mission include CISA and other DHS components, HHS and FDA, VA, Treasury and IRS, DOE, State, USDA, DOT, and FAA.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Procurement and Contract Vehicles. Own the path to contract, not just the path to yes. Structure deals across GSA MAS, NASA SEWP, and CIO-SP, work through resellers and distributors, including Carahsoft, and know when sole source is defensible and how to build the justification with the customer. Run RFI and RFP responses end-to-end, and plan backward from end-of-fiscal-year buying cycles rather than being surprised by them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Buying Committee. Map and work with the full committee: the program office that owns the requirement, the CISO and CIO organizations that own the risk, and the contracting officer who owns the money. Identify early which of your relationships is a technical champion and which one can actually put funds on contract, and build a plan to get both. Multithread deliberately and document who is missing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compliance and Authorization Realities. Know how FedRAMP status, ATO timelines, and agency-specific security review gate a deal, and set expectations with customers and internally rather than discovering the gate at the finish line. Speak fluently to the regulatory drivers that create the requirement, including EO 14028, the OMB software security memos, and CISA guidance on SBOM. Turn those drivers into a business case a program office can defend in a budget conversation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partnering Across the Company. Work with sales engineering to scope pilots and evaluations that prove the point quickly, with marketing on agency-specific campaigns and event presence, and with the CRO on deal strategy and pricing. Bring your partners into deals early. You are an individual contributor, not a solo operator.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Field Signal Back to Product. Bring back what you hear: unmet requirements, competitive gaps, procurement friction, the reasons deals stall. Feed it to the product team and to the Head of Federal Sales in a form that can be acted on. What gets built and how it gets sold should go hand in hand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Forecast Discipline and CRM Rigor. Keep the CRM current and honest, with real next steps, real close dates, and a defensible reason for every stage. Forecast within a tight band and call your own slips before they are asked about. This is not administrative work; it is how the company plans hiring and spending.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You Bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years selling enterprise software, with meaningful time in the federal civilian sector. You have carried a federal number and hit it. You have sold technical security software, not adjacent IT, and you can describe deals you built from first contact to award.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cybersecurity domain knowledge. Working fluency in software supply chain risk, SBOM, vulnerability management, and compliance. You understand the security buyer&#39;s world well enough to run a technical discovery call without an SE in the room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Procurement and contract vehicle fluency. Direct experience closing through GWACs and schedules, working with resellers and distributors, and building sole-source justifications. You know how a requirement becomes a solicitation and how a solicitation becomes an award.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-sourced pipeline track record. You have built territory from scratch without BDR support, ideally at an early-stage vendor. You can point to specific accounts you opened yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Buying committee navigation. Demonstrated ability to work with program offices, CISO and CIO organizations, and contracting shops in parallel, and to distinguish between influence and authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with authorization gates. Experience selling a product through FedRAMP status questions and ATO processes, and setting realistic timelines around them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecast rigor. Disciplined pipeline management and accurate forecasting. You are rigorous about your own data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-accelerated workflow. AI is part of how you research accounts, prepare for calls, and draft responses. You can point to concrete output and to the judgment you apply before anything goes to a customer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency. Strong bias to action, comfortable owning outcomes end-to-end in an intense, resource-constrained environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships inside civilian agencies where software supply chain security is already a funded priority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as the first or earliest federal seller at a startup, before a vehicle or past performance existed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SBOM and AIBOM and the regulatory drivers behind them, including EO 14028, the OMB software security memos, and FDA premarket cybersecurity requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work with Carahsoft or comparable federal distribution partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture-style experience shaping requirements before a solicitation is released.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary of $140,000 – $175,000, with total on-target earnings of up to $280,000 including performance-based variable compensation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Location&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a fully remote role, with a preference for candidates currently residing in the DMV area. Travel to clients is expected as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully remote&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO (taken seriously)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance — 100% covered for you and your dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) and retirement options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;About Manifest&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manifest is on a mission to secure the global software and AI supply chain. Our platform automates the discovery and analysis of risks across internally built and third-party software and AI systems, giving security, product, and engineering teams complete visibility into the components and dependencies that make up their technology stack. From product security and AI risk to supplier risk and compliance, we help teams trust the software and AI they build and buy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded by alumni from the Department of Defense, CISA, and Palantir, Manifest is backed by leading investors including Ensemble VC, First Round Capital, Homebrew, BoxGroup, XYZ Venture Capital, AE Ventures, Leap435, and Overmatch VC. The company partners with the US Air Force, DHS, Global 2000 companies, and critical infrastructure organizations across defense, automotive, and financial services to bring transparency, resilience, and trust to modern digital systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Manifest is seeking an experienced Infrastructure Engineer to own the design, development, implementation, and ongoing operation of Manifest&#39;s infrastructure and build/release pipelines. You will extend and improve existing processes and systems, ensuring pipelines are fast, secure, performant, and scalable. By dogfooding Manifest&#39;s core products, you will be closely involved with Product, driving roadmap direction and helping users build and deliver software with less risk and greater security.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;This role requires an active Top Secret/Sensitive Compartmented Information (TS/SCI) clearance.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Own the design, development, implementation, and ongoing operation of infrastructure and build/release pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Extend and improve existing processes to ensure pipelines are fast, secure, performant, and scalable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Deploy IaC and automation (Terraform, Ansible, Helm, Go, etc.) to support platform and customer requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Operate and sustain cloud-based CI/CD pipelines using DevSecOps principles and a shift-left mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Automate application deployment using container technology (Kubernetes, GitHub, and other CI/CD tools)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Build tools and packaging to support deployment across varied environments (AWS, Azure/GCP, on-prem, air-gapped, FedRAMP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Integrate DevSecOps tools and services into automated pipelines throughout the customer SDLC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Research and adopt open-source tools to build and secure the development pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Implement and improve observability across MELT (Metrics, Events, Logs, Traces), including presentation and alerting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Safely expose public endpoints (UIs, APIs) using load balancers, CDNs, and related tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Collaborate closely with Product to help drive roadmap direction and improve how users build and deliver software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Dogfood Manifest&#39;s core products as part of day-to-day work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Assisting developers in delivering secure applications (CORS policies, API security engineering)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;IaC and automation tools: Terraform, Ansible, Helm, Go&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Cloud-based CI/CD pipelines with a DevSecOps and automation-first approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Kubernetes — deploying, operating, and troubleshooting in cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Networking and runtime troubleshooting, including complex remote and air-gapped environments&lt;/li&gt;
